{"n": 155, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "155.webp", "text": "WORKING INSTRUCTIONS FOR ENGUNE ELECTRICAL AND IGNITION SYSTEMS\n\n(TCI = Transistor Coil Ignition and DME = Digital Motor Electronics)\n\nAlways disconnect the battery or interrupt power supply to the control unit and ignition coil\nwhen working on the electrical system, charging the battery or welding on the car — danger\nfrom primary and secondary voltage in engine and general electrical equipment (e.g. alternator)\n\nNever start the engine after removing the distributor cap or disconnecting the wire on ignition\ncoil terminal 4 — pull off plug on ignition control unit.\n\nNever disconnect the battery or wires on the alternator and starter while the engine is runrung.\n~ Only use specified original BMW parts.\nNever connect a shielded capacitor or test lamp on terminal 1 of the ignition coil,\n\nNever connect terminal 1 of the ignition coil with ground or B +. Consequently when service\ninstalling a burglar alarm system, the terminal 1 wire must not be used for startér interlocking.\n\n~ Pull off the control unit plug in cars with TCI or the fuel injection master relay (relay 2) in\ncars with DME when checking the compression.\n\nThe secondary (high voltage) side of the ignition system must be shielded with at least 4 k-ohms,\nwhereby the original distributor rotor with 1 k-ohm must be installed. Never use a 5 k-ohm\ndistributor rotor for interference suppression of a radio or communication set!", "words": [["WORKING", 0.2655, 0.0703, 0.3207, 0.0822], ["INSTRUCTIONS", 0.3252, 0.0703, 0.4078, 0.0822], ["FOR", 0.4119, 0.071, 0.4341, 0.0822], ["ENGUNE", 0.4382, 0.071, 0.4802, 0.0842], ["ELECTRICAL", 0.4853, 0.071, 0.5562, 0.0822], ["AND", 0.5598, 0.0716, 0.5846, 0.0822], ["IGNITION", 0.5887, 0.071, 0.6408, 0.0822], ["SYSTEMS", 0.6444, 0.071, 0.6955, 0.0822], ["(TCI", 0.2665, 0.0869, 0.2877, 0.0988], ["=", 0.2923, 0.0902, 0.2974, 0.0942], ["Transistor", 0.3014, 0.0869, 0.3495, 0.0981], ["Coil", 0.3531, 0.086